# iOS app scope (mandatory)

## Product boundary

**Sarrafi Cars iOS** (`ios/`) is a separate native app, not the website. The website is `frontend/` + server-rendered templates.

## Where to edit

| Task | Edit only |
|------|-----------|
| SwiftUI screens, navigation, filters, maps | `ios/SarrafiCars/SarrafiCars/**` |
| iOS docs, architecture, API notes | `ios/**` |
| Xcode project | `ios/SarrafiCars/SarrafiCars.xcodeproj/` |

## Where NOT to edit (iOS-only tasks)

- `frontend/templates/`, `frontend/static/` — website
- `backend/listings/routes.py`, listings HTML — website
- Unrelated `backend/` refactors, dealer tools, scanners

## Backend exception

Touch `backend/main.py` (or mobile tests) **only** when the user explicitly needs a new/changed **JSON API** for the app. For backend-only iOS work, follow **backend-ios-api-scope** (`.cursor/rules/backend-ios-api-scope.mdc`):

1. Minimal API diff only.
2. Update `ios/docs/API_CONTRACT.md` and `backend/mobile/contract.py`.
3. Follow `docs/SECURITY_MASTER_TODO.md` for auth/CSRF work.

## Module layout (see `ios/ARCHITECTURE.md`)

- `App/` — entry, tabs, `AppConfig`, `AppState`
- `Core/Theme`, `Core/Components` — shared UI
- `Networking/` — `APIClient`, `Models`
- `Features/<Feature>/` — one folder per tab/flow
- `Web/` — WKWebView embeds only
- `Resources/` — plist, assets
- `Legacy/` — not compiled; do not revive without request

## Do not

- Move iOS logic into `frontend/static/main.js` or listings templates.
- Add iOS-only UI to the website “for parity” unless the user asks for website work.
- Put new Swift files in the flat `SarrafiCars/` root — use the feature folders above.
